r=add(138,'Carrot Soup with Long-Simmered Beef-Bone Stock',6,270,'Beef bones, onion and turnip enrich the stock before carrots are cooked in it and sieved into a smooth soup.',[stock(2000),I('bones',500,'g','food-grade beef soup bones','Omit the bones and use a rich prepared beef stock; flavor differs.'),onion(200),turnip(150),carrot(600),salt(),pepper(),cayenne()],['Put {{stock}}, {{bones}}, quartered {{onion}}, diced {{turnip}}, {{salt}} and {{pepper}} in a large saucepan. Bring to a gentle simmer, skim any foam, cover loosely and simmer for 3 hours. Add water as needed to keep the bones covered.','Strain through a fine sieve into a clean saucepan. Discard the bones and spent vegetables, checking carefully that no bone fragments remain.','Thinly slice {{carrot}}, add to the strained stock and simmer for 30–45 minutes until very soft. Press the carrots and liquid through a sieve, using the whole peeled carrot.','Return to the pan with {{cayenne}} and simmer uncovered for 10–20 minutes until the soup is as thick as desired. Stir often; serve warm.'],'A smaller modern batch supplies a bone weight and uses 600 g carrots for a fuller consistency. The full three-hour stock enrichment is retained. Whole peeled carrots replace outer flesh only. Serving immediately is permitted; making it a day ahead is optional and requires prompt refrigeration, not room-temperature storage.')
r=add(139,'Slow Butter-Stewed Carrot Soup',8,140,'Carrots soften slowly in butter before a second gentle simmer in stock, giving a smooth soup with a rich carrot flavor.',[carrot(907),butter(85),stock(2000),salt(),cayenne(),water(60)],['Cut {{carrot}} into 6 mm slices. Melt {{butter}} in a heavy saucepan over low heat. Add the carrot slices and {{water}}, cover and cook very gently for 1 hour, stirring every 10 minutes. Keep them from browning; add a small splash of water if the pan begins to dry.','Add {{stock}} and simmer, partly covered, for 45–60 minutes until the carrots are completely soft.',PUREE,'Add {{salt}} and {{cayenne}}. Simmer gently for 5 minutes, skim any foam and serve.'],'The source two pounds carrot and three ounces butter become rounded modern 907 g and 85 g. The stock is standardized to 2 L. A small measured water addition and a lid protect the source long butter-stewing stage from scorching; the distinctive two-stage method remains.')
